## 3. Java

```java
public class BinarySearch {
    /**
     * Returns the index of target in a sorted array, or -1 if not found.
     *
     * @param arr   sorted array (ascending)
     * @param target value to search for
     * @return index of target or -1
     */
    public static int binarySearch(int[] arr, int target) {
        int left = 0;
        int right = arr.length - 1;

        while (left <= right) {
            int mid = left + (right - left) / 2; // avoid overflow
            if (arr[mid] == target) {
                return mid;
            } else if (arr[mid] < target) {
                left = mid + 1;
            } else {
                right = mid - 1;
            }
        }
        return -1; // not found
    }

    // Demo
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[] data = {11, 22, 33, 44, 55, 66};
        System.out.println(binarySearch(data, 44)); // 3
        System.out.println(binarySearch(data, 7));  // -1
    }
}
```

